# Confirmation Report: Orientation Day Refreshments and Equipment Delivery

**Author:** François Dubois  
**Date:** March 25, 2026  
**Context:** Confirmation report of delivered refreshments and equipment for the orientation day.

---

## Overview
This report provides a detailed confirmation of the successful delivery of refreshments and equipment required for the upcoming orientation day. The logistics team has ensured that all items are accounted for and meet the specified requirements. This delivery supports the smooth execution of the event scheduled to take place on **March 30, 2026**.

---

## Delivery Summary

### **1. Refreshments**
The following refreshments were delivered and verified:

- **Beverages**:
  - 200 bottles of still water (500ml each)
  - 150 bottles of sparkling water (500ml each)
  - 100 bottles of assorted fruit juices (330ml each)
  - 50 cans of soft drinks (variety pack, 330ml each)

- **Snacks**:
  - 100 individually wrapped granola bars (assorted flavors)
  - 75 packets of assorted nuts (30g each)
  - 50 bags of pretzels (50g each)

- **Special Dietary Options**:
  - 20 gluten-free snack packs
  - 15 vegan-friendly snack packs
  - 10 nut-free snack packs

All refreshments were delivered in temperature-controlled containers to ensure freshness. Expiry dates were checked, and all items are valid through at least **April 15, 2026**.

---

### **2. Equipment**
The following equipment was delivered and verified:

- **Audio/Visual (A/V) Equipment**:
  - 2 portable PA systems with wireless microphones
  - 1 projector and screen setup
  - 3 laptop docking stations with HDMI support

- **Seating and Tables**:
  - 50 folding chairs (padded, black finish)
  - 10 rectangular folding tables (6 ft each)

- **Signage and Stands**:
  - 5 portable signboards for directional guidance
  - 3 retractable banners with event branding

- **Miscellaneous**:
  - 200 lanyards with name tag holders
  - 5 large trash bins with recycling compartments
  - 10 packs of disposable tablecloths (white, 54"x108")

Each item was inspected for functionality and completeness. The logistics team confirmed that all equipment is operational and meets quality standards.

